Wow. Most of these don't make any sense to me at all. Mostly, the
things I #adjust are tools, because I find myself [a]pplying them
often, and armor, once I get a relatively stable set. FWIW, here's my
list:

k - key, lock pick, or credit card. Often the first one I #adjust,
                                    because I use it all the time.
b - bag (0bviously, when I can get it, a BoH).
t - towel or blindfold (because of 'b' above and 'B' below).
w - whistle (never bother to keep one unless it's a magic whistle).
l - light source of any kind
u - unihorn
c - expensive camara
s - stethoscope
p - pick-axe or other digging tool (used to use 'e', because
                                    it's the archaeologist's
                                    starting pick-axe slot)

A - Armor (Capitals used here because [W]ear uses a capital
           letter for the command)
B - Boots
C - Cloak
G - Gauntlets
H - Helm
T - T-shirt or Hawaiian shirt
R - Robe
W - Mummy Wrapping

d - dagger or dart (or sometimes arrows; just throwing weapons)
a - often, primary weapon (because it's usually your starting weapon
                           slot)

As you can see, my scheme is often related to function rather than
specific item. It doesn't matter if I'm using a lock pick or credit
card; it's a [k]ey as far as I'm concerned.

For most everything else, I use menus. I #adjust these because I find
myself using them all the time.
